WEBVTT

00:00:00.487 --> 00:00:05.931
Journey five: sign in and out. A member signs in, stays signed in

00:00:05.931 --> 00:00:11.460
safely, and signs out. This run takes the journey from seventy-six

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.135
percent to complete.

00:00:13.992 --> 00:00:17.897
A visitor on Legacy Financial's page presses Message.

00:00:17.897 --> 00:00:22.834
Jubilee asks them to join or sign in first, and remembers what they

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:23.424
started.

00:00:24.126 --> 00:00:28.685
They sign in, and they are back on the same listing with the message

00:00:28.685 --> 00:00:33.312
dialog open. The same holds for booking a meeting, asking for a quote

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:34.854
and requesting an item.

00:00:35.557 --> 00:00:41.221
A save works the same way. A visitor presses the heart and signs in.

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:45.469
The business is saved once, and the heart shows it.

00:00:46.172 --> 00:00:50.294
Now a draft. A member writes a message to Trevor.

00:00:50.294 --> 00:00:54.668
Before they send it, the session ends on the server.

00:00:55.372 --> 00:01:00.711
They press Send. The app keeps what they typed on this device, closes

00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:04.271
the dialog and opens the session-expired page.

00:01:04.271 --> 00:01:08.140
The Sign in link carries the address to return to.

00:01:08.847 --> 00:01:13.885
After signing in, the dialog is open again with the message in it, and a

00:01:13.885 --> 00:01:18.713
notice says: We kept what you typed. Nothing is sent until the member

00:01:18.713 --> 00:01:19.623
presses Send.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.437
Every form a member writes in keeps its draft this way: requests, the

00:01:25.437 --> 00:01:30.105
reply box of a conversation, a report, feedback, the profile and the

00:01:30.105 --> 00:01:34.774
owner's editors. A draft holds no password and no file, stays on the

00:01:34.774 --> 00:01:39.099
device for thirty days, is restored once, and is removed when a

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.884
different member signs in.

00:01:41.718 --> 00:01:46.901
On the account page, the Sign out section now says where the member is

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:50.306
signed in: on this phone and one other device.

00:01:50.306 --> 00:01:53.046
Sign out of other devices asks first.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:59.511
They confirm. Every other session ends, this one stays, and the section

00:01:59.511 --> 00:02:05.030
says: signed in on this phone only. The button is no longer offered.

00:02:05.732 --> 00:02:11.475
Sign out asks too. It ends this session only and lands on the welcome

00:02:11.475 --> 00:02:16.885
page. An unsent draft is kept at sign-out and returns to the same

00:02:16.885 --> 00:02:17.468
member.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.065
Behind the screen, two more criteria are proved.

00:02:22.065 --> 00:02:27.191
When several calls are refused for one ended session, together or one

00:02:27.191 --> 00:02:30.980
after another, the session-expired page opens once.

00:02:31.836 --> 00:02:37.280
And outside development the session cookie is now issued with the host

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.469
prefix: secure, HTTP-only, same-site lax.

00:02:40.469 --> 00:02:45.991
The app, the marketing site and the admin application each call the API

00:02:45.991 --> 00:02:50.036
on their own origin, so no other origin is approved.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.836
Seventeen API test cases prove both.

00:02:53.692 --> 00:02:58.442
Decision record forty-six holds these decisions, and journey five is

00:02:58.442 --> 00:03:03.331
complete. Left for the owner: the visual, responsive and accessibility

00:03:03.331 --> 00:03:08.011
sweeps. The list of sessions with their location belongs to journey

00:03:08.011 --> 00:03:11.644
twenty, and token redaction in logs to journey four.
